  "extraction_notes": "DMF and HCONH2 are listed as reagents because they serve as the formyl group source. In cases where no other solvent is specified (Nguyen 2012 and This Study), they also serve as the reaction medium. In the Sheppard 2013 reaction, MeCN is explicitly listed as the solvent. Catalyst 1 is bis(2-chlorophenyl)borinic acid. For the amine reactant, [1*] and [2*] represent R1 and R2 substituents. If R2 is H, it represents a primary amine; if R2 is non-H, it represents a secondary amine."
